atom:['Atomic structure','CHEMISTRY · PHYSICS','Explore a simplified Bohr atom. Select any of the 118 elements to update its atomic number and model.',['Nucleus|Contains protons and neutrons and nearly all atomic mass.','Electron shells|Simplified energy levels; real electrons are described by quantum states.'],'Atomic number equals proton count; a neutral atom has the same number of electrons.'],
water:['Water molecule · H₂O','CHEMISTRY · MOLECULES','One oxygen atom bonded to two hydrogen atoms in a bent geometry.',['Oxygen|Central atom; electron distribution makes water polar.','Hydrogen|Shares electron pairs with oxygen.','Covalent bonds|Shared electron pairs hold atoms together.'],'The H–O–H angle is about 104.5 degrees.'],
methane:['Methane · CH₄','CHEMISTRY · MOLECULES','A tetrahedral molecule with one carbon and four hydrogen atoms.',['Carbon|Forms four covalent bonds in this model.','Hydrogen|Four outer atoms arranged around carbon.'],'Methane is the main component of natural gas.'],
co2:['Carbon dioxide · CO₂','CHEMISTRY · MOLECULES','A linear molecule with carbon between two oxygen atoms.',['Carbon|Central atom.','Oxygen|Each forms a double bond with carbon in this simplified model.'],'CO₂ is used in photosynthesis and absorbs infrared radiation.'],
engine:['Cutaway combustion engine','MECHANICAL SYSTEMS','Inspect a simplified engine. Select a part or use EXPLODE to separate the components.',['Cylinder block|Main structural body housing cylinders.','Piston|Moves up and down under gas pressure.','Connecting rod|Transfers piston motion to the crankshaft.','Crankshaft|Converts reciprocating motion into rotation.','Valves|Control intake and exhaust flow.','Spark plug|Ignites the compressed mixture in spark-ignition engines.'],'Educational schematic, not a dimensionally accurate engineering CAD model.'],
gears:['Gear train','MECHANICAL SYSTEMS','Two meshing gears transfer rotation; the larger driven gear turns more slowly.',['Driver gear|Input gear supplies torque.','Driven gear|A simple external gear pair rotates in opposite directions.','Gear teeth|Transfer force while reducing slip.'],'For ideal gears, speed ratio is inverse to tooth-count ratio.'],
motor:['Electric motor','ELECTRICITY · MACHINES','A rotor turns inside a stator as magnetic forces create torque.',['Stator|Stationary magnetic field source.','Rotor|Rotating assembly attached to the shaft.','Coil|Current in a magnetic field experiences force.','Shaft|Carries rotational motion to a load.'],'Real motors use different designs and control circuits.'],
pendulum:['Simple pendulum','PHYSICS · MOTION','Watch gravitational potential energy convert to kinetic energy and back.',['Pivot|Suspension point.','String|Constrains the bob to an arc.','Bob|Mass driven by gravity.'],'For small swings, T ≈ 2π√(L/g).'],
lever:['Lever & fulcrum','PHYSICS · MACHINES','A lever trades applied force for distance.',['Fulcrum|Pivot about which the lever rotates.','Effort arm|Distance from pivot to applied force.','Load|The resistance being moved.'],'Ideal balance: effort × effort arm = load × load arm.'],
solar:['Solar system','SPACE · PHYSICS','A schematic planetary system. Sizes and distances are not to scale.',['Sun|The star at the centre of our system.','Planets|Orbit the Sun under gravity.','Orbit paths|Illustrative, not precision ephemerides.'],'Gravity governs most planetary motion.'],
combustion:['Combustion reaction','CHEMISTRY · REACTIONS','Balanced equation: CH₄ + 2O₂ → CO₂ + 2H₂O. Atoms rearrange; they are not created or destroyed.',['Reactants|Methane and oxygen.','Products|Carbon dioxide and water.','Energy|Combustion releases heat and light.'],'Limited oxygen can produce carbon monoxide or soot.'],
photosynthesis:['Photosynthesis','BIOLOGY · CHEMISTRY','6CO₂ + 6H₂O + light → C₆H₁₂O₆ + 6O₂, a simplified overall equation.',['Carbon dioxide|Carbon source for plants.','Water|Supplies electrons and hydrogen; oxygen is released.','Light|Energy captured by chlorophyll.'],'The complete process includes many steps in chloroplasts.'],
projectile:['Projectile motion','PHYSICS · KINEMATICS','A launched object follows a parabolic path under constant gravity; air resistance is omitted.',['Initial velocity|The launch speed sets the horizontal and vertical components.','Gravity|A constant downward acceleration curves the path.','Trajectory|Horizontal velocity is constant in this ideal model.'],'Ideal vacuum model: no drag, spin, wind, or lift.'],
spring:['Spring–mass oscillator','PHYSICS · OSCILLATIONS','A mass oscillates on a spring; the ideal model follows Hooke’s law with no damping.',['Spring|Restoring force is proportional to displacement in the linear range.','Mass|Inertia determines how quickly the system responds.','Equilibrium|The mean position where net force is zero.'],'Ideal oscillator: x(t) = A cos(ωt); real springs have damping and nonlinearity.'],
collision:['Elastic collision','MECHANICS · MOMENTUM','Two equal masses approach, collide, and separate; the idealized collision conserves momentum and kinetic energy.',['Momentum|Total momentum is conserved in an isolated system.','Contact|The collision transfers momentum between the bodies.','Kinetic energy|Conserved for a perfectly elastic collision.'],'This is a schematic equal-mass, one-dimensional collision.'],
circuit:['Electric circuit','PHYSICS · ELECTRICITY','A battery drives conventional current around a closed circuit with a resistor and LED.',['Battery|Provides a potential difference.','Resistor|Limits current and dissipates electrical energy as heat.','LED|A diode emits light when forward biased.','Electrons|Drifting charge carriers move opposite to conventional current.'],'Illustrative low-voltage circuit; component values and current are not to scale.'],
ammonia:['Ammonia · NH₃','CHEMISTRY · MOLECULES','Ammonia has a trigonal-pyramidal molecular geometry around nitrogen.',['Nitrogen|Central atom with a lone electron pair.','Hydrogen|Three hydrogen atoms form polar covalent bonds.','Molecular geometry|The lone pair makes the shape pyramidal.'],'Approximate H–N–H bond angle is 107 degrees.'],
